      "30": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "POWER\nThis node gives the input to the power of N\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n•  The Saw oscillator is set to unipolar in the inspector. This provides us with values running from 0 to 1 before jumping back to 0.\n• The output of the oscillator modulates the radius of the yellow ring.\n• The output is also sent to the Power node, where it computes itself to the 5th power.\n• This results in the red ring expanding half way through the motion of the yellow ring but manages to catch up in the end.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 216.98385620117188,
          "width": 924.6085205078124,
          "x": 94.59823608398438,
          "y": 169.40411376953125
